Three questions that will help me narrow this down

1. When a new account gets blocked, does the provider say suspicious activity, account disabled, identity verification required, or something else?

2. Are you using the same computer and internet connection when creating replacement accounts?

3. Did cybersecurity give you a case number or written acknowledgment of your report?

I’m particularly interested in the exact error messages. They can help distinguish account-security flags, identity verification problems, and actual evidence of unauthorized access.

You deserve a way to communicate, manage your appointments, and access your own accounts without repeatedly getting stuck in recovery loops.
